    "what": "Same source fact as ARC-020 D5 (root counted once; PROBE-HOOK-01): before a `dotnet add/remove reference` runs, K1 blocks unless the edge is an accepted decision, L0 blocks every reference command, L1 asks the user, M1 and K0 deny until a self-written marker is added, M allows and reminds afterwards. The five gated candidates release on different conditions, so they are mutually incomparable. The dependency-command gate, which also bears on Reserved question 1, is scored once at DEP-004 (RC-ENF-DEP-INSTALL-GATE).",
